<?xml version="1.0"?>
<ScenContainer xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema">
  <ScenTitle>SC Mauritania Pt 3, 2011</ScenTitle>
  <ScenDescription>&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;&lt;P&gt;&lt;EM&gt;[The Strike Commander saga continues in Mauritania.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Follows &lt;STRONG&gt;SC Mauritania Pt&amp;nbsp;2 - 2011&lt;/STRONG&gt;]&lt;/EM&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Background&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;BLOCKQUOTE style="MARGIN-RIGHT: 0px" dir=ltr&gt;
&lt;P&gt;The past twenty years has seen unprecedented world-wide upheaval with the uncivil fracturing of the Soviet Union, failed interventions in the Mid-East and continental environmental disasters.&amp;nbsp; Across the globe&amp;nbsp;old political orders fall, energy resources dwindle&amp;nbsp;and economies collapse.&amp;nbsp; Mercenaries become a commonplace tool as governments and powerful corporations vie among each other to protect or assert their interests.&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BLOCKQUOTE&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Mauritania, July 2011&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;BLOCKQUOTE style="MARGIN-RIGHT: 0px" dir=ltr&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Struggling with an externally-funded rebellion, the leadership of the North African nation of Mauritania has turned to employing&amp;nbsp;private military&amp;nbsp;forces to stem their losses.&amp;nbsp; The Turkish-based &lt;STRONG&gt;Wildcats&lt;/STRONG&gt;, a mercenary fighter squadron composed of F-16 fighters, has been retained and is&amp;nbsp;flying from a remote Strike Base in the Western Sahara.&amp;nbsp; &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Things in Mauritania have heated up.&amp;nbsp; A right-wing military element has staged a coup, toppling the rightful government, and aligned itself with the rebels.&amp;nbsp; With enemies on all sides and no one left to pay the bills, the Wildcats are forced to face cutting their losses and running.&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BLOCKQUOTE&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;</ScenDescription>
